{{- /* "true" or "false": is this a personal machine?

       The profile set is the source of truth; this is the shell-facing face of
       it, exactly as .chezmoitemplates/is-container is for the container half.
       Scripts write

           is_personal={{ includeTemplate "is-personal" . }}

       and get a bare word. Calling `contains` at the site instead puts
       parentheses in the rendered line, which shellcheck cannot parse — the
       same reason is-container exists rather than a stat call per script. */ -}}
{{- if contains " personal " (includeTemplate "profiles" .) -}}true{{- else -}}false{{- end -}}
